    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d543">

                <pb facs="0736" n="724" sameAs="frus:frus1945v05/pg724"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">811.248/1–1345: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of State to the Ambassador in
                        Spain</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Hayes</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1945-01-13T22:00:00-04:00">January 13,
                            1945—10 p.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>88. The War Department desires to obtain the permission of the Spanish Government
                    to make landings in Madrid of planes of the Air Transport Command on regularly
                    scheduled flights from the United States to Paris and Rome. As Mr. George<anchor
                        n="79" xml:id="d543-f1"/> is thoroughly familiar with this project he is
                    being sent to Madrid, accompanied by Colonel Payne,<anchor n="80"
                        xml:id="d543-f2"/> to assist you. They expect to leave Washington the
                    morning of the 16th by transport plane and to proceed via Casablanca. Depending
                    on connections, they probably will travel to Lisbon by air from Casablanca.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Grew</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d543-f1" n="79" xml:id="d543-f1-content">
                <p>William Perry George, Assistant Chief of the Division of Western European
                    Affairs.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d543-f2" n="80" xml:id="d543-f2-content">
                <p>Lt. Col. Robert G. Payne of the Air Transport Command.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
